WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.063
Journey twenty-two: read policies and get help.

00:00:04.063 --> 00:00:09.146
Members read the statement of faith, the terms, the privacy notice and

00:00:09.146 --> 00:00:14.301
help. New in this run: an administrator publishes a new version of each

00:00:14.301 --> 00:00:17.714
from the admin application, with no deployment.

00:00:18.578 --> 00:00:23.471
Policies lists the four pages, each with its published version, and when

00:00:23.471 --> 00:00:25.442
and by whom it was published.

00:00:26.143 --> 00:00:28.969
Edit opens the published text in fields.

00:00:28.969 --> 00:00:33.913
The preview beside them shows the draft as members will read it, dated

00:00:33.913 --> 00:00:36.103
today, and follows each change.

00:00:38.746 --> 00:00:44.105
Publish asks first. Members read it at once, version two is kept, and

00:00:44.105 --> 00:00:47.290
the publish is recorded in the audit log.

00:00:47.992 --> 00:00:53.388
Version three is published. The editor now starts from it, and every

00:00:53.388 --> 00:00:55.768
earlier version is kept below.

00:00:57.147 --> 00:01:01.875
A member opening the privacy notice reads the new version straight away.

00:01:02.925 --> 00:01:06.866
Behind the screen, the tests prove that a publish started from an older

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:10.863
version is refused and nothing is published; that each publish is stored

00:01:10.863 --> 00:01:14.694
with the administrator's name and audited; that only an administrator

00:01:14.694 --> 00:01:18.635
reaches these screens; and that members read the pages from a cache the

00:01:18.635 --> 00:01:22.077
publish clears, which still answers when the database is down.

00:01:22.939 --> 00:01:27.457
What is left is the owner's: the real privacy contact and the final

00:01:27.457 --> 00:01:31.435
legal wording, published from Policies, with no deployment.
